From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jianfeng Liu <Jianfeng.Liu@cixtech.com>
Date: Sat, 10 Oct 2026 15:00:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 78/92] usb: cdns3: fix xhci timeout at resume from STR

On resume from STR, cdnsp_controller_resume() ran the
cdns_power_is_lost() check while the controller was still in platform
suspend, because cdnsp_set_platform_suspend(dev, false, false) was
only called later in the resume path.  The power-lost check could
therefore read a wrong value, conclude that no power was lost, and
skip the controller re-initialization - the xhci device then timed
out on resume.

Move cdnsp_set_platform_suspend(cdns->dev, false, false) to the very
start of the resume path, before the power-lost check.

Signed-off-by: Jianfeng Liu <Jianfeng.Liu@cixtech.com>
---
 drivers/usb/cdns3/cdnsp-plat.c | 4 ++--
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/usb/cdns3/cdnsp-plat.c b/drivers/usb/cdns3/cdnsp-plat.c
index 8e7ea7d0b..21c4a31e1 100644
--- a/drivers/usb/cdns3/cdnsp-plat.c
+++ b/drivers/usb/cdns3/cdnsp-plat.c
@@ -332,6 +332,8 @@ static int cdnsp_controller_resume(struct device *dev, pm_message_t msg)
 	if (!cdns->in_lpm)
 		return 0;
 
+	cdnsp_set_platform_suspend(cdns->dev, false, false);
+
 	if (cdns_power_is_lost(cdns)) {
 		phy_exit(cdns->usb2_phy);
 		ret = phy_init(cdns->usb2_phy);
@@ -348,8 +350,6 @@ static int cdnsp_controller_resume(struct device *dev, pm_message_t msg)
 	if (ret)
 		return ret;
 
-	cdnsp_set_platform_suspend(cdns->dev, false, false);
-
 	/* cdns_resume() may sleep; do not invoke it under cdns->lock. */
 	cdns_resume(cdns);
 
